  "details": "I want a graph in-game that will tell me generally what is giving me the most lag.\n\nLike an in-game Task Manager, it will tell me how much player avatars are taking up my CPU/GPU, how much goes to networking, how much goes to the world itself.\n\nThat way people can KNOW whether or not the world is causing lag, or if it's somebody with a specific avatar, or if it's just all avatars in general.\n\nThis would be useful to everyone.\n\nCreators would more easily be able to figure out what causes lag.\n\nPeople just hanging out in a public world could instantly tell who's avatar is causing the most lag, and hide it if necessary from the menu.\n\nWe already have a system for automatically hiding Very Poor avatars, but if a more real-time statistic could be made, this functionality could be improved.",
